Subject: [PATCH] riscv: use fixed-width trap vectors for all CLIC channels

Vectored traps enter at BASE + 4 * cause. Prevent compressed jumps from
shrinking slots, and cover IDs 0 through 47 (16 internal plus 32 external
CLIC interrupts). This also supports implementations that retain standard
vectored mode when CLIC mode is requested.

--- a/cpukit/score/cpu/riscv/riscv-exception-handler.S
+++ b/cpukit/score/cpu/riscv/riscv-exception-handler.S
@@ -60,9 +60,15 @@
  */
 TYPE_FUNC(_RISCV_Vector_table)
 SYM(_RISCV_Vector_table):
-	.rept 32
+	/* Vectored traps use BASE + 4 * cause, even with the C extension.
+	 * Cover the 16 internal and 32 external CLIC interrupt IDs (0..47).
+	 */
+	.option push
+	.option norvc
+	.rept 48
 	j .LRISCV_Exception_handler
 	.endr
+	.option pop
 
 .LRISCV_Exception_handler:
 	addi	sp, sp, -CPU_INTERRUPT_FRAME_SIZE
